      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KING OF DRAGONS (7) was only beaten a length in a BM72 at Canterbury. The move back from mid-week company reads well and he appears the likely leader of the field. JVO can dictate from the front and he'll be tough to mow down on his recent figures. I'VE BEAN TRYIN' (1) is the class counterpoint, returning after three months with strong 1400m credentials. Wasn't disgraced at Caulfield after some good efforts in prior at Hawkesbury and Randwick. Drawn nicely and can fire. CANDO ATTITUDE (5) has not fired in two runs this campaign, but her overall record is still sharp and she gets to a more suitable assignment third-up. BLOW IN (3) has the current form, winning a BM68 at Hawkesbury after a close third at this venue on resumption. Boasts a strong third-up record and McDougall's booking is a big tick. stablemate LAUREL HILL (2) draws the inside again with the blinkers being reapplied and can't be left out of calculations.",
